{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774739,"nonce":"MXdVlDYmpPV/4qpB5sIweZOKWW8=","title":"fix(dogfood): file-mounted App PEM, .scarab guidance, App-config prerequisites (03ef8e4, 245a99c, 70aa42e)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #81 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/dogfood-infra-and-runbook` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T18:05:51Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T18:14:55Z\n\nCloses git-bug `03ef8e4`, `245a99c`, `70aa42e`. Three commits, one per ticket. **No Rust touched.**\n\nTwo of the three were already partly or wholly fixed on `main` — what remained in each case was delivery or documentation, not code.\n\n---\n\n**Already fixed on `main`** (`f32cd74`): the rule is narrowed to `/.scarab/*` with negations for `*.yaml`, `*.yml` and `lib/`, and `.scarab/ci.yaml`, `.scarab/dogfood.yaml`, `.scarab/lib/notify.yaml` are all tracked.\n\nProven: `git check-ignore -v` on those three exits 1 with no match, while `.scarab/objects/ab/deadbeef` is still matched. An audit of what actually writes under `.scarab/` at runtime found exactly one thing — the dev object store (`SCARAB_OBJECT_DIR`, default `./.scarab/objects`) — so the current rule is correct as-is.\n\nWhat remained was the ticket's second half: nothing told a *downstream* repo author that `.scarab/` is tracked source. Adds a caution where the directory is introduced in the pipeline-syntax docs — the pipeline is read from the triggering commit, a local server writes its object store into the same directory, so ignore `/.scarab/objects/` specifically and never `/.scarab`.\n\n---\n\n**The server side already ships in full, and none of it was re-implemented.** Verified: both `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM` and `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM_FILE` in config with unit tests · inline wins over file · an unreadable path is a loud boot failure (ADR-0048), mirroring the OIDC signing key · the boot PEM overrides the DB `_forge` credential in App mode · and the startup credential audit correctly skips GitHub connections when a boot PEM is present, so an absent `_forge` secret isn't reported DEGRADED.\n\nThe real gap was **delivery**. The chart offered the PEM only as an env var — key material passing through Helm values, no file-mount path at all — and `deploy/local-helm/deploy.sh` never used it, so the dogfood loop still seeded the PEM through `reseed.sh`'s `POST /v1/secrets`: exactly the bootstrap ordering the ticket filed.\n\n- Chart: `secrets.githubAppPemSecret.{name,key}` projects an out-of-band Secret read-only at `/etc/scarab/forge/\u003ckey\u003e` (mode 0440, root:65532) and sets `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM_FILE`. One helper (`scarab.githubAppPemPath`) so the ConfigMap and Deployment can't disagree.\n- `deploy.sh` maintains that Secret from the `SCARAB_APP_PEM` path already in `.env`; `reseed.sh` detects the mount from the deployed Pod spec and skips its PUT, leaving it responsible only for installation registration.\n- Documented in the chart README, `deploy/local-helm/README.md`, `.env.example`, and the public Installation page.\n\nVerified independently: with the Secret configured, `helm template` renders the volume, the read-only mount and `SCARAB_GITHUB_APP_PEM_FILE: \"/etc/scarab/forge/github-app.pem\"`. **The default render contains zero references to any of it**, so existing deployments are unaffected. `helm lint` clean, `bash -n` on both scripts.\n\n---\n\n`deploy/local-helm/README.md` already carried a thorough version, so no new doc was created. The gap was the two places someone *actually configures an App*:\n\n- `docs/handoffs/dogfood-scarab-on-scarab.md` listed events and permissions as flat bullets with no warning. Now states Push + Pull request subscription and `Commit statuses: read \u0026 write` as REQUIRED, each with its silent-failure mode — an empty subscription list still delivers `installation` / `installation_repositories`, so `/v1/repos` looks healthy while nothing ever runs; a missing statuses grant 403s every post while the run goes green.\n- The public Helm install page had **no App prerequisite at all** — a live-cluster operator never reads the local-helm README.\n\nVerified with a real `astro build`: 133 pages, clean, both asides present in the rendered HTML.\n\n---\n\nThe ticket's optional part (b) — a `/v1` preflight/doctor that mints an installation token and diffs granted permissions and subscribed events against what Scarab needs. That's a feature, not a runbook fix, and wants its own ticket.\n\n`cargo check --workspace` clean (no Rust changed) · `helm template` both states + `helm lint` · `git check-ignore -v` · `astro build`. Integrated with the other three dogfood branches: **597 passed, 21 ignored**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}